2026-08-25T00:00:00Z (RFD66606-2016) 'Checking sccache
 # uuid: 0ab8453f-cfa5-54a6-8ffb-ab95e76a1299
 # tags: rfd:title
 RFD:Committed  1 RFD
 Serials:VSekaiFabric

2026-08-25T00:00:01Z (RFD66606-2016) 'One command shows whether the shared sccache bucket is really in use.
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD2016  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:02Z (RFD66606-2016) 'The failure mode is silent: if the `SCCACHE_*` environment is missing, the credentials are wrong, or the region/endpoint is off, sccache quietly falls back to a local disk cache, or records read/write errors, while the build still succeeds.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2016  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-2016) 'Run `sccache --show-stats` after a build and check that `Cache errors` reads 0.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2016  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-2016) 'Checking sccache
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2016  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-2016) '`sccache --show-stats` is how anyone confirms the cache is healthy, and `Cache errors 0` after a build is the confirmation that the bucket, region and credentials are all right. Nothing else proves it: a misconfigured sccache falls back to local disk and the build still succeeds, so "the build worked" is not evidence the cache worked.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2016  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2016) '- RFD66606-2017 compiles the engine through this cache.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2016  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2016) 'Context and Problem Statement
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2016  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-2016) 'Native builds route compilation through sccache (https://github.com/mozilla/sccache) backed by a shared DigitalOcean Spaces bucket (`chibifire-sccache`, region `tor1`), so object files are cached across machines and CI (see `rfd/2017-compiling-godot-engine/index.md`). The failure mode is silent: if the `SCCACHE_*` environment is missing, the credentials are wrong, or the region/endpoint is off, sccache quietly falls back to a local disk cache, or records read/write errors, while the build still succeeds. The shared-cache benefit is lost with no obvious signal. How does someone confirm sccache is actually using the remote bucket and is healthy?
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2016  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-2016) 'Decision Drivers
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2016  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-2016) '- A misconfigured cache degrades silently (local disk, or errored requests) without failing the build, so "the build worked" is not evidence the cache worked.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2016  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-2016) '- The check should be one command, not a ritual or a log dive.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2016  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-2016) '- Credentials are scoped to the `do-tor1` AWS profile, not global environment variables, so the check must not require exporting secrets.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2016  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:13Z (RFD66606-2016) '- It should read the same on Windows (PowerShell) and WSL/Linux.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2016  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:14Z (RFD66606-2016) 'Considered Options
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2016  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:15Z (RFD66606-2016) '- Infer from build times (implicit, unreliable, no backend visibility).
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2016  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:16Z (RFD66606-2016) '- Enable `SCCACHE_LOG=debug` and read the per-request log every build.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2016  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:17Z (RFD66606-2016) '- Read `sccache --show-stats` and check the backend and error counters.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2016  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:18Z (RFD66606-2016) 'Windows PowerShell wrapper
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2016  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:19Z (RFD66606-2016) 'Aliases cannot carry logic, hence a function plus a `Set-Alias` shim:
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2016  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:20Z (RFD66606-2016) '```powershell
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2016  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:21Z (RFD66606-2016) 'function sccheck {
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2016  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:22Z (RFD66606-2016) '    sccache --show-stats |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2016  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:23Z (RFD66606-2016) '        Select-String -Pattern 'Compile requests|Cache hits|Cache misses|Cache .*errors|Cache location'
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2016  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:24Z (RFD66606-2016) '}
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2016  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:25Z (RFD66606-2016) 'Set-Alias scc sccheck
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2016  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:26Z (RFD66606-2016) '```
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2016  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:27Z (RFD66606-2016) 'The bash equivalent is `sccache --show-stats` filtered with `grep`. To measure a single build, reset first: `sccache --zero-stats; <build>; sccache --show-stats`.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2016  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:28Z (RFD66606-2016) 'Consequences
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2016  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:29Z (RFD66606-2016) '- Good: one command shows the backend and health; no secrets needed, since stats read the running server's own counters.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2016  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:30Z (RFD66606-2016) '- Good: works identically across shells; the PowerShell `sccheck`/`scc` shortcut makes it a reflex.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2016  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:31Z (RFD66606-2016) '- Bad: the counters are per-server-session, they reset when the sccache server restarts or on `--zero-stats`, so they are not lifetime bucket totals.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2016  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:32Z (RFD66606-2016) '- Bad: `--show-stats` alone does not prove S3 connectivity; only a compile (or a full build) exercises read/write. `Cache errors = 0` after a build is the real confirmation that auth and the endpoint are correct.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2016  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:33Z (RFD66606-2016) 'Confirmation
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2016  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:34Z (RFD66606-2016) 'Running `sccheck` reported `Cache location  s3, name: chibifire-sccache, prefix: /godot/`, `Cache errors 0`, and hits accumulating during a Godot rebuild, so the remote backend, region, and `do-tor1` credentials are all working.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2016  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:35Z (RFD66606-2016) 'More Information
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2016  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:36Z (RFD66606-2016) 'Native builds route through sccache against `chibifire-sccache`, and `scons` keeps its own cache alongside it. That pairing is settled; an install that forgets the `SCCACHE_*` environment is an installation defect rather than an open question.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2016  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:37Z (RFD66606-2016) '- The non-secret `SCCACHE_*` variables (`SCCACHE_BUCKET`, `SCCACHE_ENDPOINT`, `SCCACHE_REGION`, `SCCACHE_S3_USE_SSL`, `SCCACHE_S3_KEY_PREFIX`) are set globally; credentials live in the `do-tor1` profile (`~/.aws/credentials`) and are applied only for the duration of a build, so the real AWS CLI is never shadowed.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2016  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:38Z (RFD66606-2016) '- Per-project key prefixes keep objects from colliding in the one bucket (e.g. `godot` vs `idtx-flow`).
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2016  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:39Z (RFD66606-2016) '- To debug a non-zero error count, set `SCCACHE_LOG=debug` and `SCCACHE_ERROR_LOG` in the sccache service launcher and reinstall the service so the supervised server picks them up (`decisions/20260606-windows-background-services-nssm.md`).
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2016  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:40Z (RFD66606-2016) 'The problem
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2016  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:41Z (RFD66606-2016) 'Native builds route compilation through sccache (https://github.com/mozilla/sccache) backed by a shared DigitalOcean Spaces bucket (`chibifire-sccache`, region `tor1`), so object files are cached across machines and CI (see `rfd/2017-compiling-godot-engine/index.md`).
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2016  1 LINE
 Text:Written
